course: dictionary
lesson: 6720
title: Officially
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Officially» tells you that something has been approved or announced by someone in charge, or by the rules. A school is officially opened when the right people say it is open. A record is officially broken when the judges agree.
explain: In the news, «officially» can show what was announced, which may not be the whole truth: «Officially he resigned, but really he was pushed out.» When you see «officially», ask yourself: who said this, and did they have the power to say it?
explain: Children also use «officially» as a joke to make a big statement. «I'm officially starving!» does not mean the rules say you are hungry. It means you are really and truly hungry, and you want everyone to know it.
fact: Officially means in a way that is approved by people in charge, or according to the rules or the law.
fact: Officially can also mean in public, according to what has been announced, even if the truth may be different.
fact: In a joke, «I'm officially starving» means really and truly starving.
fact: A spokesperson speaks officially for a group, so they speak with the group's approval.
fact: Useful phrases: «officially opened», «officially announced», «it's official».
exercise: «The new library was officially opened by the mayor on Monday.» What does officially mean here? | *Approved by the people in charge | Whispered quietly | Only pretend, as a joke | Very late
exercise: Sam says, «I'm officially starving!» What does officially mean? | Only on a Monday | Slowly | In a secret way | *Really and truly
exercise: «Officially, the match was called off because of rain.» Why might the word officially matter? | It means the rain was heavy and cold | It means the match was very fun | It means the match was played on grass | *It shows what was announced, which may not be the whole truth
test: «A spokesperson speaks officially for a group.» What does this mean? | Speaks only about food | Sings for fun | *Speaks with the group's approval, as its chosen voice | Speaks quietly in a corner
test: What is a school that is «officially opened»? | One that opened by accident | One that opened for only one day | *One opened in the way the people in charge have approved | One that is closed forever
exam: Which sentence uses «officially» in the joking, informal way? | *I'm officially starving! | The council officially approved the new park. | The rules say you must wear a helmet, officially. | The school was officially opened by the mayor.
